      en: "The Ceylon Fishery Harbours Corporation (CFHC) is a state entity tasked with developing and managing fishery harbours across Sri Lanka. It oversees more than 20 harbours and landing sites, providing essential facilities such as cold storage, ice plants, fuel stations, and slipways. The CFHC supports the fishing industry, which employs over 500,000 people directly and indirectly. It ensures that fish catches are handled efficiently, reducing post-harvest losses. The corporation also operates fish markets and promotes exports. Over the past decade, CFHC has modernized several harbours with new infrastructure to boost productivity and safety.",
